iled-to-object-to-numerous-instances-of-prejudicial-prosecutorial-argument-i-the-sixth-amendment-to-the-united-states-constitution-guarantees-a-i-criminal-washington)948 0 R(proposition-vi-prison-resulting-from-the-trial-courts-ordering-all-eighteen-individual-sentences-to-be-served-consecutively-amounts-to-an-unconstitutionally-excessive-sentence-i-an-excessive-sentence-is-one-which-either-exceeds-the-statutory-maximum-or-which-under-the-facts-and-circumstances-of-a-given-case-is-so-excessive-as-to-i-shock-the-conscience-of-the-court-see-watts-v-state-2008-ok-cr-27-1-10-194-i-p3d-133137-the-question-of-excessiveness-a-study-of-all-the-facts-and-circumstances)949 0 R(proposition-vii-the-accumulation-of-error-in-this-case-deprived-appellant-of-due-process-of-law-in-violation-of-the-fifth-and-fourteenth-amendments-to-the-united-states-constitution-and-article-ii-7-of-the-oklahoma-constitution-i-even-if-none-of-the-previously-discussed-errors-can-when-viewed-in-isolation-i-necessitate-reversal-of-appellants-conviction-the-combined-effect-of-these-errors-deprived-him-of-a-fair-trial-and-requires-that-his-conviction-be-reversed-see-skelly-i-v-state-1994-ok-cr-55-880-p2d-401-407-peninger-v-state-1991-ok-cr-60-811-p2d-609613-gooden-v-state-1980-ok-cr-76617-p2d-248-249-250-some-of-these-i-errors-were-not-properly-preserved-for-appellate-review-however-this-court-has-i-found-that-objections)950 0 R(statement-of-facts)943 0 R(statement-of-the-case)942 0 R]>>>>>>
